---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="USPS Mail Kiosks Bid & Discovery" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href="/projects" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>USPS Mail Kiosks Bid & Discovery</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Led generative and evaluative research for a high-stakes government and enterprise bid focused on an older demographic.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">USPS Operations</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Lead researcher</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Mixed methods, competitive intelligence, AI-accelerated wireframing</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Understanding accessibility and adoption barriers in self-service kiosk systems</h2>
          <p>The challenge was understanding how diverse users, particularly older adults, interact with self-service postal kiosks and what barriers prevent adoption. This required balancing compliance requirements with user needs and competitive positioning.</p>
          <p>Through a combination of generative research and competitive evaluation, we identified key pain points and validated requirements that informed the bid strategy. The research helped position the client to select a partner and requirements that would serve a broad demographic effectively.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
